			"date": "2024-03-28T14:11:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> not entirely related to the article, but I believe, developer tools should also focus on reducing size and compute overhead. </p><p>Going by <a href=\"https://www.11ty.dev/docs/performance/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">11ty.dev/docs/performance/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> , 11ty have like 34mb of node_module while gatsby (biggest piece of horseshit I've ever used 🤮🤮) have half a gb for the same.</p>",
