			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Lohr (RIP Natenom)",
				"url": "https://chaos.social/@lexLohr",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/330/724/126/125/304/original/714e1989a9748224.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T14:46:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The web itself is fast. Ads and their tracking, unnecessary feature cruft, frameworks needlessly throwing objects around and trying to take more control of the DOM than necessary and a lack of deferred loading strategy make it slow.</p>",
