			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T15:37:27.536Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@JackEvans\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>JackEvans</span></a></span> Failure is temporary as we move away from tools that have proven to be less than ideal—I remain optimistic!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112174227913048430",
			"parentId": "112173716126123999",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112174227897024455",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T16:21:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> Looking at node_modules size is a silly measure of bloat. Adding a great build tool like esbuild as a dependency, for example, downloads native binaries for every platform and so is huge. Does that mean using esbuild is bad and your project is bloated?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112174308524321674",
			"parentId": "112174227913048430",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112174308524321674",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T16:41:52.005Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> I would acknowledge that the original post (on front-end performance) does not strictly relate to node_modules size, installation, or build performance.</p><p>I would argue that node_modules size is worth measuring!</p><p>As to whether “software bloat” extends to your dependencies, I would also argue that it does! More dependencies, more maintenance.</p><p>I’m assuming there is a relationship between dependency count and file size, here. Maybe not with esbuild, but generally.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112174333292205978",
			"parentId": "112174308524321674",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112174333212324121",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T16:48:08.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> Agreed, so let me reword what I said:</p><p>*Only* looking at node_module size is a silly measure of bloat. (Because the entirety of it might be something like native binaries for multiple platforms).</p><p>34MB could be 1000 terrible dependencies. 500MB could be one great dependency. The size, entirely on its own, is only a hint and it’s super silly to dunk on a package for that alone.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112174367711457282",
			"parentId": "112174333292205978",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112174367711457282",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T16:56:55.131Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> that might be true!</p><p>My hunch is that those are outliers and not typical—but maybe!</p><p>Someone should do a <a href=\"https://github.com/wooorm/npm-esm-vs-cjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/wooorm/npm-esm-vs-c</span><span class=\"invisible\">js</span></a> -style analysis but for dependency count versus file size! 👀</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112175053041841881",
			"parentId": "112174367711457282",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112175053027351045",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T19:51:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> Surely. But the existence of outliers tells us node_modules size is (at most) correlational with good build speeds and small output bundles. It is not causal.</p><p>Meanwhile, web page payload size has a *causal* relationship with performance.</p><p>The distinction is important if this isn’t to be some silly aesthetic preference, which I suspect for some people it is.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112175144509952147",
			"parentId": "112175053041841881",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112175144509952147",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-28T20:14:28.133Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span> ah hmm—well, this doesn’t fit my experience. It doesn’t seem to fit the example cited in <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@nrk9819\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>nrk9819</span></a></span>’s original post either?</p><p>Either way I’m fine with disagreeing on a thing (and I’ve hit my text reply limit here)—appreciate the discussion!</p><p>(Though I suspect we agree more than this discussion might suggest!)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
